Chapter: RealTrapping
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `Real trapping` traps when a result leaves the finite range, on a NaN or on
 either infinity. This half of the coverage is the negative control: every
 value here is finite, several of them by a very small margin, and none may
 trap. A guard that fired on anything near the boundary would kill this test
 rather than fail it, which is a loud failure and the point of choosing
 these operands.

 The positive half cannot live here. A trap is a `UD2` and takes the machine
 with it, so it has no output to compare; `real-trapping-overflow` carries it
 behind a `.fatal` sidecar, the same split `bounded-param-trap` already uses.

 This test used to add 3.0 and 4.0 and nothing else. That exercised addition,
 not the mode: it never produced a NaN or an infinity, which is the only
 thing trapping is for, and the emitter checked for NaN alone and ignored
 infinity entirely for as long as the mode existed.

 Bit patterns, not decimals: the largest finite double and infinity render
 alike, and the near-boundary operands below have no short decimal form.

Section: Operands

  real-max : Real
  real-max = bits-to-real #7FEFFFFFFFFFFFFF

  real-min : Real
  real-min = bits-to-real #FFEFFFFFFFFFFFFF

Section: Ops

  add-trap : Real trapping, Real trapping -> Real trapping
  add-trap (a) (b) = a + b

  sub-trap : Real trapping, Real trapping -> Real trapping
  sub-trap (a) (b) = a - b

  mul-trap : Real trapping, Real trapping -> Real trapping
  mul-trap (a) (b) = a * b

  div-trap : Real trapping, Real trapping -> Real trapping
  div-trap (a) (b) = a / b

  trap-bits : Real trapping -> Integer
  trap-bits (x) = real-to-bits (from-real-trapping x)

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("sum " & show (trap-bits (add-trap (to-real-trapping 3.0) (to-real-trapping 4.0))))
    print-line-uni ("diff " & show (trap-bits (sub-trap (to-real-trapping 3.0) (to-real-trapping 4.0))))
    print-line-uni ("at-max " & show (trap-bits (add-trap (to-real-trapping real-max) (to-real-trapping 0.0))))
    print-line-uni ("half-max " & show (trap-bits (mul-trap (to-real-trapping real-max) (to-real-trapping 0.5))))
    print-line-uni ("max-cancels " & show (trap-bits (sub-trap (to-real-trapping real-max) (to-real-trapping real-max))))
    print-line-uni ("min-at-edge " & show (trap-bits (sub-trap (to-real-trapping real-min) (to-real-trapping 0.0))))
    print-line-uni ("div-small " & show (trap-bits (div-trap (to-real-trapping real-max) (to-real-trapping 2.0))))
  end
